(4341422, 625654, 83067, '<td valign="top">great detail in the feathers. without the beak, the image isn''t drawing me places...</td>', 'great detail in the feathers. without the beak, the image isn''t drawing me places...', '2007-12-28 16:13:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(4341425, 625468, 83067, '<td valign="top">feels like the monolith from 2001: A Space Odyssey</td>', 'feels like the monolith from 2001: A Space Odyssey', '2007-12-28 16:14:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(4341428, 624827, 83067, '<td valign="top">leaf, building, bricks, one image, two... This one keeps you guessing, great job!</td>', 'leaf, building, bricks, one image, two... This one keeps you guessing, great job!', '2007-12-28 16:15:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(4341433, 625139, 83067, '<td valign="top">nice choice of color tones to compensate for the slightly soft focus. it works in an old-fashion sort of way</td>', 'nice choice of color tones to compensate for the slightly soft focus. it works in an old-fashion sort of way', '2007-12-28 16:16:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(4341434, 625821, 83067, '<td valign="top">nice DOF and color hues</td>', 'nice DOF and color hues', '2007-12-28 16:17:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(4341435, 625267, 70689, '<td valign="top">The pic seems to be shaken and is fairly noisy. It has several pixelations, probably due to overprocessing or local overexposure. It also seems that the pic has a reddish cast, implying that your white balance is off. <br/> <br/>It seems to me you tried to take a pic under conditions that your camera is not fit for. In this specific case, you might have used a tripod (or stack of books) to allow for a longer shutter time (@lower ISO), to get ridd of the shake and noise. You may adjust the white balance either in camera or in pp. Wish you more luck next time.</td>', 'The pic seems to be shaken and is fairly noisy. It has several pixelations, probably due to overprocessing or local overexposure. It also seems that the pic has a reddish cast, implying that your white balance is off.  It seems to me you tried to take a pic under conditions that your camera is not fit for. In this specific case, you might have used a tripod (or stack of books) to allow for a longer shutter time (@lower ISO), to get ridd of the shake and noise. You may adjust the white balance either in camera or in pp. Wish you more luck next time.', '2007-12-28 16:17:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(4341436, 625817, 70689, '<td valign="top">Nice pic, realy like the perspective and use of shallow DOF. Too bad the bokeh seems so noisy.</td>', 'Nice pic, realy like the perspective and use of shallow DOF. Too bad the bokeh seems so noisy.', '2007-12-28 16:18:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(4341438, 624329, 83067, '<td valign="top">the cake looks good, the goo/icing on the fork is distracting in a aqua-rusting sort of way.</td>', 'the cake looks good, the goo/icing on the fork is distracting in a aqua-rusting sort of way.', '2007-12-28 16:19:20.000000', NULL, 1),
